  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers RFC 9116 security.txt: the /.well-known/security.txt file served over HTTPS as text/plain; charset=utf-8, every field in the IANA security.txt Fields registry (including CSAF and Bug-Bounty), OpenPGP cleartext signing with Canonical, the ABNF and parsing limits, and the section 5 security considerations. It lists two version lines: RFC 9116 (current, with its errata) and draft-foudil-securitytxt -00 to -12 (legacy, upgraded from). SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out versions and upgrades, fields, serving and signing, and parsing and security.",
